config.yaml
config.local.yaml
frontend/node_modules/

# Agent worktrees live here; they are checkouts, not sources.
.claude/
__pycache__/

# The console bundle is BUILT, not committed. It was committed so that
# `go build` needed no Node toolchain -- and it cost 29 MB of history,
# about seventy per cent of this repository, because a minified bundle
# is a new blob on every dependency bump. Worse, a committed artifact
# can go STALE without anything failing: v0.14.0 shipped a console
# reading a protobuf field the server no longer sent. A missing bundle
# is a compile error (`pattern all:dist: no matching files found`);
# a stale one is a silent bug, and committing it chose the silent one.
#
# `just build` builds it first.
frontend/dist/

# Same rule, same reason: generated, so not in git. The published npm
# package is this repository's root, built by the release workflow and
# published to GitHub Packages at the tag's version. (Building it on a
# git install through `prepare` did not survive yarn 4, which packed the
# dependency without running it and shipped no ts/dist.)
ts/dist/

# The documentation site build (mkdocs.yaml) and its privacy-plugin cache.
/_site/
/.cache/
